Nor98</article-title><source>Vet Rec</source><year>2004</year><volume>155</volume><fpage>636</fpage><lpage>637</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15573787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>EFSA</collab></person-group><article-title>Opinion of the scientific panel on biological hazards on classification of atypical transmissible spongiform encephalopathy (TSEs) cases in small ruminants</article-title><source>The EFSA Journal</source><year>2005</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>30</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bruce</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name><name><surname>Nonno</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldmann</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Di Bari</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Esposito</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Benestad</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Agrimi</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nor98-like sheep scrapie in the United Kingdom in 1989</article-title><source>Vet Rec</source><year>2007</year><volume>160</volume><fpage>665</fpage><lpage>666</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17496276</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Baylis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Chihota</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Stevenson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldmann</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sivam</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Tongue</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Gravenor</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Risk of scrapie in British sheep of different prion protein genotype</article-title><source>JGV</source><year>2004</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>2735</fpage><lpage>2740</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1099/vir.0.79876-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dawson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoinville</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hosie</surname><given-names>BD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Guidance on the use of PrP genotyping as an aid to the control of clinical scrapie</article-title><source>Vet Rec</source><year>1998</year><volume>142</volume><fpage>623</fpage><lpage>625</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9650232</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9650232</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tongue</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfeiffer</surname><given-names>DU</given-names></name><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Elliot</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>del Rio Vilas</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Estimation of the relative risk for developing clinical scrapie: the role of prion protein (<italic>PrP</italic>) genotype and selection bias.</article-title><source>Vet Rec</source><year>2006</year><volume>158</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>50</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16415231</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>EFSA</collab></person-group><article-title>Report of the working group on the breeding programme for TSE resistance in small ruminants</article-title><source>The EFSA Journal</source><year>2006</year><volume>382</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>46</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>L&#x000fc;hken</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Buschmann</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Groschup</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Erhardt</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prion protein allele A(136)H(154)Q(171) is associated with high susceptibility to scrapie in purebred and crossbred German Merinoland sheep</article-title><source>Arch Virol</source><year>2004</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>1571</fpage><lpage>1580</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15290381</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00705-004-0303-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moum</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Olsaker</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopp</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Moldal</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Valheim</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Moum</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Benestad</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Polymorphisms at codons 141 and 154 in the ovine prion protein gene are associated with scrapie Nor98 cases</article-title><source>JGV</source><year>2005</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>231</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1099/vir.0.80437-0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group pers